      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCK THE SUNRISE (4) is the safe form reference after winning a BM60 at Townsville by a neck, following a nose defeat there in BM65 grade, and his consistency keeps him right in the contest. GARINION RIGH (3) has to rebound from an 11th behind ROCK THE SUNRISE, but her prior Class 4 win at Townsville showed she can produce a sharp finish when things fall into place. ENGELINE (7) is the value inclusion: both recent runs read honestly, and the weight relief gives her a genuine chance to press for the money if she handles the rise in trip. SEALORD (8) can feature in a competitive Ewan Cup despite the drop back from 2200m being the obvious query. He was fourth at Sunshine Coast in a Class 1, beaten just over two lengths after being steadied mid-race and still picking up nicely, so there is more merit in that run than the bare placing.",
